{{Quote|This is an image from a Coruscant Security Force holocam stationed above the temple district the night of the Jedi Purge. Most of the files were erased, but I found a slicer who pulled this off a backup archive.|Jedi [[Padawan]] [[Ferren Barr]]|<ref name="Darth Vader (2017) 14">[[Darth Vader (2017) 14|''Darth Vader'' (2017) 14]]</ref>}}
The '''Palace Court''', known during the [[time]] of the [[Galactic Republic]] as the '''Jedi Temple Precinct''', the '''Temple Precinct''', or the '''Temple District''', was an area that surrounded the [[Imperial Palace]], formerly the [[Jedi]] Temple, on [[Coruscant]]. Composed of dozens of city blocks, the precinct was controlled jointly by the [[Jedi Council]] and the [[Galactic Republic]] until [[19 BBY]].

==Description==
[[File:TempleDistrict-LostFound.png|thumb|left|250px|The Jedi Temple was located in the Temple Precinct of the Core World Coruscant.]]
Around the [[time]] of the [[Clone Wars]], the Temple Precinct was a low-rise sector of the [[Federal District]] comprised of modern buildings that consisted mainly of standard accommodations. In the center of the Precinct was the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple complex]]&mdash;a conglomerate of structures built over [[Millennium|millennia]]; an [[Archaeologist|archaeological]] treasure behind which laid histories of the [[Jedi]] center's numerable instances of expansion, renovation, ruin, and reconstruction that revolved around a [[Vergence|locus of power]]: a natural mountain found sacred by [[Coruscanti]] and which attracted [[Force-sensitive|Force-wielders]] of various beliefs; an amalgamation of numerous wellsprings of [[the Force]] hidden beneath the spire's many lost grottos and shrines.<ref name="CL2016" />

Within the district was the [[Processional Way]], a long lane which terminated with ceremonial steps that led to the Jedi Temple, atop of which laid two statues each of the [[Jedi Order]]'s [[Sage Master]]s and [[Jedi Guardian|Warrior Masters]].<ref name="CL2016" /> Situated between low-rising structures, various sparsely-situated [[Jedi]] statues sat amidst the Precinct's Way.<ref name="Sabotage">{{TCW|Sabotage (episode)}}</ref> These serene features marked a Jedi tranquility distinct from the otherwise dense urban constructs cut by busy thoroughfares of the [[Imperial City|Galactic City]], with the broad promenade providing a symbolic bridge between.<ref name="CL2016" />

[[File:Aotc_1410.jpg|thumb|right|250px|The Temple Precinct was a low-rise area punctuated by a spaceport tower and the Temple itself.]]
A [[spaceport tower]] rising from the Precinct allowed for the docking of [[Starship|spaceships]] too large for the [[Temple hangar]]s&mdash;constructed within the Temple after the [[Invasion of Naboo|time]] of the [[Naboo]] [[blockade]]<ref name="CL2016" /> in [[32 BBY]]<ref name="GA">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref>&mdash;in the Jedi Temple complex. Below the monolith was an extensive collection of buildings, divided by avenues and averaged in their rise, that accommodated the standard training of [[Padawan]]s. Such low-rising structures gave the Temple, most notably its great spires, domination over the landscape for [[kilometer]]s around.<ref name="CL2016" />

The district was renamed as the Palace Court during the [[Imperial Era|reign]] of [[Galactic Emperor|Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious|Palpatine]].<ref name="NoP" /> Under the [[Monarchy|Emperor]], the precinct served as a [[Hangar|landing field]] for [[capital ship]]s, housing a courtyard with the capacity to hold multiple [[Venator-class Star Destroyer|''Venator''-]] and [[Victory-class Star Destroyer|''Victory''-class]] [[Star Destroyer]]s.<ref name="Tarkin" />

==History==
[[File:JediTemple-TZBSB.png|thumb|left|250px|During the Republic Era, the area that surrounded the Jedi Temple on Coruscant was known as the Temple Precinct.]]
The transitionary boulevard between the fringe and heart of the Jedi Temple Precinct&mdash;the Processional Way&mdash;bore witness to heated gatherings during the [[Republic Era|fall of the Republic]] and the early [[Standard day|days]] of the [[New Order]] that [[Proclamation of the New Order|took]] its place.<ref name="Sabotage" /><ref name="DLOTS 1">[[Darth Vader (2017) 1|''Darth Vader'' (2017) 1]]</ref>

During the Clone Wars, a crowd of friends and family of the casualties of the [[bombing of the Jedi Temple hangar]] gathered to stage a protest against the continuation of the war in a demonstration of [[anti-Jedi sentiment]].<ref name="Sabotage" />

Under the New Order that took the place of the Republic, [[Grand Vizier]] [[Mas Amedda]] personally hosted a [[celebration marking the eradication of the Jedi Order]] at the Palace Court. Addressing citizens gathered before the entry steps, the Imperial bureaucrat [[Lightsaber incinerator|incinerated]] fallen Jedi's [[lightsaber]]s.<ref name="DLOTS 1" /> [[Cam droid]]s<ref name="USW">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> recorded the occasion from above the gathering.<ref name="DLOTS 1" />

[[File:ImperialPalace-JediSurvivor.png|thumb|right|250px|During the Imperial Era, the Temple District was renamed the Palace Court and the Jedi Temple became the Imperial Palace.]]
The Palace grounds were transformed into a large landing field by the [[Galactic Empire]],<ref name="Tarkin" /> with a dedicated landing pad raised before the Imperial Palace's entrance for a<ref name="F&D Beta">[[Star Wars: Force and Destiny Beta|''Star Wars: Force and Destiny'' Beta]]</ref> [[Lambda-class T-4a shuttle|''Lambda''-class T-4a shuttle]].<ref name="USW" /> This was accessible via a walkway that accommodated rows of [[Color|white]]-[[Clothing|clad]] escorts and [[Emperor's Royal Guard|Imperial Royal Guardsmen]].<ref name="F&D Beta" /><ref name="IRG DB">{{Databank|imperial-royal-guard|Imperial Royal Guard}}</ref> Despite these changes, the precinct still remained a low-rise area by<ref name="ROTJ">{{Film|VI}}</ref> the outbreak of the [[Coruscant civil war|civil war on Coruscant]]<ref name="Aftermath">[[Aftermath (novel)|''Aftermath'']]</ref> in [[4 ABY]].<ref name="4 ABY">The events of ''Aftermath'' takes place immediately after that of ''Star Wars'': Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'', which is dated [[4 ABY]] by ''Star Wars: Galactic Atlas''.</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The Palace Court's first [[canon]]ical appearance was in the [[1999]] film [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']].<ref name="TPM">{{Film|I}}</ref> It was identified as the Palace Court and the Temple Precinct in the [[2016]] ''[[Star Wars: Force and Destiny]]'' sourcebook ''[[Nexus of Power]]''.<ref name="NoP" />

